# SDT ingestion skill

The knowledge pipeline in one line: sources land in `context/ingestion/`
(user), the agent distils them into `context/wiki/` pages, and consumed sources
move to `context/refs/` only after the user approves the write-and-archive
plan.

1. Read `context/instructions/ingestion.md` **before any distillation** — the
   invocation scope (`all`, one file, a glob, a URL), the routing test
   (`single-pass` vs `book-scale`) and the operating sequence live there.
2. List the scope with `sdt context ingest list`; the status is derived, never
   assumed. Convert non-markdown sources first; the converted artifact is what
   the routing test measures.
3. Write and update wiki pages per `context/instructions/wiki.md` — one concept
   per page, atomic cited claims, typed `relations`.
4. **Approve-before-archive**: present the write-and-archive plan and wait for
   the user's approval before anything leaves `context/ingestion/`. The archive
   move (pending → archived) is the only legal mutation of the immutable dirs.
5. On verification doubts, `context/instructions/distillation.md` and the
   research lane (`research.md`) own the reading discipline; this skill owns the
   pipeline gates.
